        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "848e3ff0-3f55-51ae-9b17-55dae3b5c027",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Kassir, Charlie Adler\n- Works: Reefer Madness, Tiny Toon Adventures, Rocket Power, Pocahontas, Tak and the Power of Juju, The Looney Tunes Show\n- Characters: Ralph, Buster Bunny, Ray \"Raymundo\" Rocket, Meeko, Jibolba, Pete Puma, Deadpool\n- Topics: Voice acting, Off-Broadway, film adaptation, musical satire\n\nFacts:\n- Reefer Madness is a musical satire of the 1936 cult classic \"Reefer Madness\" that opened in Los Angeles in 1998.\n- John Kassir played Ralph in the Off-Broadway show \"Reefer Madness\" and in its film adaptation.\n- John Kassir took over from Charlie Adler late in the final season of \"Tiny Toon Adventures\" to voice Buster Bunny.\n- John Kassir voiced Ray \"Raymundo\" Rocket in \"Rocket Power\".\n- John Kassir voiced Meeko in \"Pocahontas\" and its direct-to-video sequel.\n- John Kassir voiced Jibolba in the \"Tak and the Power of Juju\" video game series.\n- John Kassir is the current voice of Pete Puma in \"The Looney Tunes Show\".\n- John Kassir is the current voice of Deadpool in unnamed series mentioned in the source sentence.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
